{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::domain::Domain`. A domain is cloneable and safe to share between\nexecutions. The following chapters introduce its members one capability at a\ntime.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    type Error: Send;\n    type NodeData: Clone + Eq + Hash + Send + Sync;\n    type NodeContent: NodeContents;\n    type EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync;\n\n    fn cache(&self) -> &ValidationCache<Self>;\n    fn node_path(&self, node: &NodeId<Self>) -> NodePath;\n    fn node_content(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeContent, Self::Error>;\n    fn outgoing_edges(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        label: Self::EdgeLabel,\n    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId<Self>>, Self::Error>;\n    fn load_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Option<Record<Self::NodeData, Self::EdgeLabel>>, Self::Error>> + Send;\n    fn store_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n        record: &Record<Self::NodeData, Self::EdgeLabel>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Self::Error>> + Send;\n\n    fn project_sources(&self) -> Option<SourceProject<Self>> { ... }\n    fn source_node(\n        &self,\n        item: &OutlineData,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeData, SourceError> { ... }\n    fn source_address(&self, _data: &Self::NodeData) -> Option<OutlineData> { ... }\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately cover `requirements.sdk.domain`.\n\n**Obligations and tests**\n\n- **Trait shape and bounds.** `Domain` must be `Clone + Send + Sync`. `Error` must be `Send` only. `NodeData` must be `Clone + Eq + Hash + Send + Sync`. `EdgeLabel` must be `Clone + Send + Sync`. `NodeContent` must be `NodeContents`.\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` defines a `Relationships` domain with opaque node data, label and error types. It implements every required method (`cache`, `node_path`, `node_content`, `outgoing_edges`, `load_evidence`, `store_evidence`).\n  - Its inner `check_bounds::<G: Domain>` function compiles generic code against the declared bounds, so loosening a required bound or adding an extra one breaks the build. It also requires the `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` futures to be `Send`.\n  - The test calls these futures with a non-`Sync` error, which shows that a `Send`-only error is enough.\n  - It asserts `node_path`, `outgoing_edges` and `node_content` results, and that `Error` values are returned.\n- **Default members.** `project_sources`, `source_node` and `source_address` have default bodies.\n  - The same test asserts `project_sources()` is `None` and `source_node` returns `SourceError::Invalid`.\n  - `domain_without_project_sources_leaves_source_tools_disabled` repeats these checks on `Application` and also asserts `source_address` is `None`.\n- **Application domains implement `Domain`.** `Application`, `Memory` and `Relationships` are all used as `Domain` implementations across the contract, agent and validation tests. `public_exports_match_the_appendix` checks that the public export inventory matches the spec and that the shipping `habeas` consumer compiles against the SDK.\n- **Shareable between executions.**\n  - `concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces` runs several validators over one shared `Memory` domain concurrently. It asserts a peak concurrency of 3 and the expected stored records.\n  - `concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records` does the same for `Application` with the same criterion.\n  - `concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads` and `shared_context_allows_independent_concurrent_agent_calls` share one domain between concurrent agent calls.\n  - `later_lighter_agent_calls_preserve_the_contexts_existing_trace` checks that the context is `Send + Sync`.\n  - The `domain::<G>()` bound check covers the type-level `Clone + Send + Sync` requirement.\n\nThe remaining obligations belong to the cited chapters and refining requirements. Examples are the criteria, evidence and agent behavior that several of these tests also carry `{test}` references for. They need no separate test here.\n\nI found no requirement-violating behavior that these tests would accept.",
  "references": "1219af9c261c7c256deaf030045562c41b04d884087245d89e34d2f09aa8f735",
